# Kernel Configuration Test Cases

Kernel configuration fragments for testing spdx-diff change detection.

## Test Cases

### Safe Changes (No Warnings Expected)

| File | Description | Change Type |
|------|-------------|-------------|
| `kconfig1.cfg` | Disable built-in feature | y → n |
| `kconfig2.cfg` | Disable module | m → n |
| `kconfig3.cfg` | Convert to module | y → m |
| `kconfig4.cfg` | Convert to built-in | m → y |

### Breaking Changes (Warnings Expected)

| File | Description | Change Type |
|------|-------------|-------------|
| `kconfig5.cfg` | Enable new feature | n → y |
| `kconfig6.cfg` | Enable new module | n → m |

## Reference

The reference SBOM contains baseline kernel configuration.
Each fragment modifies specific CONFIG options to test detection.

## Usage

```bash
# Test safe change
kas build kas/image-minimal.yml:kas/kernelconfig-y-to-n.yml

# Test breaking change (expect warnings)
kas build kas/image-minimal.yml:kas/kernelconfig-n-to-y.yml

```

## Validation

Safe changes should complete without warnings.
Breaking changes (n→y, n→m) should trigger compatibility warnings.
